\\\\n&= P(X \\le 5) + P(X = 6) \\\\\n&= F(5) + P(X = 6) \\\\\n&= 0.7987 + (\\frac{7}{6})(0.63)^{6}(1 - 0.63)^{7 - 6} \\\\\n&= 0.7987 + 7 \\cdot (0.63)^{6} \\cdot (0.37)^{1} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.9606\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Since $n=7$, we have that $F(7) = P(X\\leq 7) = 1$.\n\nTherefore, our completed table looks as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.9606}$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186166494 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\displaystyle \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=7$ and $p=0.63.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n- For $F(6),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =F(5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =0.7987+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6})(0.63)^{6}(1-0.63)^{7-6} \\\\  & =0.7987+7\\cdot (0.63)^{6}\\cdot (0.37)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9606.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Since $n=7,$ we have that $F(7) = P(X\\leq 7) = 1.$\n\nTherefore, our completed table looks as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X \\leq x)$ | $0.0009$ | $0.0123$ | $0.0701$ | $0.2341$ | $0.5134$ | $0.7987$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.9606}$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166495 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.67)$ given below, compute $P(X=2)$.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0013\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0969\\,$ | $\\,0.3130\\,$ | $\\,0.6422\\,$ | $\\,0.9095\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186166495 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.67)$ given below, compute $P(X=2).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0013\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0969\\,$ | $\\,0.3130\\,$ | $\\,0.6422\\,$ | $\\,0.9095\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166495 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(2) &= P(X \\le 2) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0, 1, 2}) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0, 1}) + P(X = 2) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 1) + P(X = 2) \\\\\n&= F(1) + P(X = 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X = 2) &= F(2) - F(1) \\\\\n&= 0.0969 - 0.0170 \\\\\n&= 0.0799\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186166495 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1\\})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.0969-0.0170 \\\\  & =0.0799\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166496 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.47)$ given below, compute $P(1 \\leq X \\lt 5)$.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0222\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.4015\\,$ | $\\,0.7107\\,$ | $\\,0.9163\\,$ | $\\,0.9892\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186166496 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.47)$ given below, compute $P(1 \\leq X \\lt 5).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0222\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.4015\\,$ | $\\,0.7107\\,$ | $\\,0.9163\\,$ | $\\,0.9892\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166496 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(4) &= P(X \\le 4) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0, 1, 2, 3, 4}) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {0}) + P(X ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4}) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 0) + P(1 \\le X < 5) \\\\\n&= F(0) + P(1 \\le X < 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1 \\le X < 5) &= F(4) - F(0) \\\\\n&= 0.9163 - 0.0222 \\\\\n&= 0.8941\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186166496 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0\\})+P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0)+P(1\\le X<5) \\\\  & =F(0)+P(1\\le X<5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X<5) & =F(4)-F(0) \\\\  & =0.9163-0.0222 \\\\  & =0.8941.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166497 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(7, 0.52)$ given below, compute $P(X \\geq 2)$.\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0059\\,$ | $\\,0.0504\\,$ | $\\,0.1951\\,$ | $\\,0.4563\\,$ | $\\,0.7393\\,$ | $\\,0.9233\\,$ | $\\,0.9897\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186166497 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(7, 0.52)$ given below, compute $P(X \\geq 2).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0059\\,$ | $\\,0.0504\\,$ | $\\,0.1951\\,$ | $\\,0.4563\\,$ | $\\,0.7393\\,$ | $\\,0.9233\\,$ | $\\,0.9897\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166497 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a)\n$$\n\nNow, note that\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 2) = P(X \\gt 1)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\ge 2) &= P(X > 1) \\\\\n&= 1 - P(X \\le 1) \\\\\n&= 1 - F(1) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.0504 \\\\\n&= 0.9496\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186166497 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 2) = P(X \\gt 1).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X>1) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =1-F(1) \\\\  & =1-0.0504 \\\\  & =0.9496.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166726 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425542 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166727 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425543 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166727 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425546 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166728 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425540 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166728 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425544 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166729 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425541 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186166729 1038 #edb/ref 17592186425545 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186167034 1050 660.0 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186167141 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186167141 1071 "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6, 0.26)$. Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X \\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $0.8144$ | $0.9569$ | $0.9944$ | $0.9997$ | $1.0000$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186167141 1071 "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.26).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing values in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $\\,0.8144\\,$ | $\\,0.9569\\,$ | $\\,0.9944\\,$ | $\\,0.9997\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186167141 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.26.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing elements of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6} \\\\  & ≈0.1642.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{0})(0.26)^{0}(1-0.26)^{6-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{1})(0.26)^{1}(1-0.26)^{6-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.26)^{0}\\cdot (0.74)^{6}+6\\cdot (0.26)^{1}\\cdot (0.74)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.5104.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186168156 1064 "When performing certain types of statistical tests (e.g., hypothesis testing), we often need to use standard cumulative distribution function (CDF) tables to carry out the test.\n\nIn this lesson, we'll learn how to construct CDF tables for the binomial distribution and use them to calculate probabilities.\n\nFirst, recall that the probability mass function of the binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\binom{n}{x} \\, p^x (1-p)^{n-x}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots, n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success.\n\nAlso, recall that the CDF of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's compute the value of $F(x)$ for the distribution $B(5,0.37)$ at $x=0$ and $x=1$.\n\nTo do that, we use the definition of the cumulative distribution function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(0) &= P(X \\le 0) \\\\\n&= P(X = 0) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{5}{0})(0.37)^{0}(1 - 0.37)^{5 - 0} \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (0.37)^{0} \\cdot (0.63)^{5} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.0992 \\\\\nF(1) &= P(X \\le 1) \\\\\n&= P(X = 0) + P(X = 1) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{5}{0})(0.37)^{0}(1 - 0.37)^{5 - 0} + (\\frac{5}{1})(0.37)^{1}(1 - 0.37)^{5 - 1} \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (0.37)^{0} \\cdot (0.63)^{5} + 5 \\cdot (0.37)^{1} \\cdot (0.63)^{4} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.3907\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe CDF data is usually presented as a table. If we were to continue this process and calculate $F(2), F(3), F(4)$, and $F(5)$, our table would look as follows:\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,\\bbox[gainsboro, 3pt]{\\color{blue}0.0992}\\,$ | $\\,\\bbox[gainsboro, 3pt]{\\color{blue}0.3907}\\,$ | $\\,0.7330\\,$ | $\\,0.9340\\,$ | $\\,0.9931\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $F(x)$ is an increasing function.\n- Since $n$ is the largest possible value of the binomial distribution, we have $F(n) = 1$." 13194139534556 17592186045417 false] [17592186168156 1064 "When performing certain types of statistical tests (e.g., hypothesis testing), we often need to use standard cumulative distribution function (CDF) tables to carry out the test. \n\nIn this lesson, we'll learn how to construct CDF tables for the binomial distribution and use them to calculate probabilities. \n\nFirst, recall that the probability mass function of the binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\binom{n}{x} \\, p^x (1-p)^{n-x}, \\qquad x=0,1,2,\\ldots, n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trials, and $p$ is the probability of success.\n\nAlso, recall that the CDF of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's compute the value of $F(x)$ for the distribution $B(5,0.37)$ at $x=0$ and $x=1.$  \n\nTo do that, we use the definition of the cumulative distribution function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =P(X\\le 0) \\\\  & =P(X=0) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0})(0.37)^{0}(1-0.37)^{5-0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.37)^{0}\\cdot (0.63)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.0992 \\\\ F(1) & =P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0})(0.37)^{0}(1-0.37)^{5-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1})(0.37)^{1}(1-0.37)^{5-1} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0.37)^{0}\\cdot (0.63)^{5}+5\\cdot (0.37)^{1}\\cdot (0.63)^{4} \\\\  & ≈0.3907.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe CDF data is usually presented as a table. If we were to continue this process and calculate $F(2), F(3), F(4),$ and $F(5),$ our table would look as follows:\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,\\bbox[gainsboro, 3pt]{\\color{blue}0.0992}\\,$ | $\\,\\bbox[gainsboro, 3pt]{\\color{blue}0.3907}\\,$ | $\\,0.7330\\,$ | $\\,0.9340\\,$ | $\\,0.9931\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\nNote the following:\n\n- $F(x)$ is an increasing function.\n\n- Since $n$ is the largest possible value of the binomial distribution, we have $F(n) = 1.$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425512 1080 "0.0504" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425512 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425512 1083 #uuid "08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425513 1080 "0.9011" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425513 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425513 1083 #uuid "0ade8b6c-624a-50a4-bad2-15e70c431679" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425514 1080 "0.7330" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425514 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425514 1083 #uuid "1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425515 1080 "0.0989" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425515 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425515 1083 #uuid "363c6137-dca5-587b-9559-70490db1b35a" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425516 1080 "0.9984" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425516 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425516 1083 #uuid "3b049551-1d9e-51e1-a8e6-dd6c16d4ea52" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425517 1080 "0.3077" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425517 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425517 1083 #uuid "4368e1e2-68d4-5d71-8fdb-de90614b84c6" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425518 1080 "0.6794" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425518 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534556 17592186045417