true] [17592186425542 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425536 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425542 1069 "q-224505" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425542 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425542 1071 "Consider the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.65).$ Rounding to $4$ decimal places, fill in the missing value in the cumulative distribution function table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $0.0018$ | $0.0223$ | $0.1174$ | $0.3529$ | $0.6809$ | {{field-1}} |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425542 1072 #uuid "45075cea-f15c-5084-914d-ebb143f8bab5" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425542 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nThe probability mass function for the Binomial distribution $B(n,p)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\\,x=0,1,2,…,n.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $n=6$ and $p=0.65.$ \n\nTherefore, we compute the missing element of the table as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =0.6809+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{5})(0.65)^{5}(1-0.65)^{6-5} \\\\  & =0.6809+6\\cdot (0.65)^{5}\\cdot (0.35)^{1} \\\\  & ≈0.9246.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425543 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425535 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425543 1069 "q-224517" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425543 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425543 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.85)$ given below, compute $P(X<5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0000\\,$ | $\\,0.0001\\,$ | $\\,0.0012\\,$ | $\\,0.0121\\,$ | $\\,0.0738\\,$ | $\\,0.2834\\,$ | $\\,0.6794\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425543 1072 #uuid "84b86fdf-72f2-5ecd-9ec1-a3a6650f805e" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425543 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(4) \\\\  & =0.0738.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425544 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425537 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425544 1069 "q-225123" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425544 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425544 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.63)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0069\\,$ | $\\,0.0660\\,$ | $\\,0.2670\\,$ | $\\,0.6093\\,$ | $\\,0.9008\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(2<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425544 1072 #uuid "af275350-4175-5761-af0d-7b660329cfde" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425544 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =1.0000-0.2670 \\\\  & =0.7330.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425545 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425538 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425545 1069 "q-225190" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425545 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425545 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(5,0.79)$ given below, compute $P(X>3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0004\\,$ | $\\,0.0081\\,$ | $\\,0.0659\\,$ | $\\,0.2833\\,$ | $\\,0.6923\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425545 1072 #uuid "b6ff4041-b681-52c7-96bc-3e966d10e527" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425545 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-0.2833 \\\\  & =0.7167.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425546 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425533 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425546 1069 "q-224526" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425546 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425546 1071 "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X=3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0198\\,$ | $\\,0.1293\\,$ | $\\,0.3820\\,$ | $\\,0.6930\\,$ | $\\,0.9083\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=3)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425546 1072 #uuid "c7cc6a15-4009-5db6-878e-1743f9fb14e2" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true] [17592186425546 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X=3) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(X=3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =F(3)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6930-0.3820 \\\\  & =0.3110.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534556 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-08b0954c-0b0f-5d90-bc97-b401944c0b15" 17592186425512 "answer-0ade8b6c-624a-50a4-bad2-15e70c431679" 17592186425513 "answer-1686d601-47e1-567a-99f3-65018bc5b85f" 17592186425514 "answer-363c6137-dca5-587b-9559-70490db1b35a" 17592186425515 "answer-3b049551-1d9e-51e1-a8e6-dd6c16d4ea52" 17592186425516 "answer-4368e1e2-68d4-5d71-8fdb-de90614b84c6" 17592186425517 "answer-45c1d3ae-7aea-5878-b0b0-750018287438" 17592186425518 "answer-4d21eaac-b64d-59c5-a232-eec231b01fdd" 17592186425519 "answer-557c159a-30a2-562f-a119-f39d2d4ff550" 17592186425520 "answer-62630e8d-d2db-5fcf-a9ee-7b86c738a8c0" 17592186425521 "answer-630e58a3-661e-52d8-a8d1-903e9b5e6179" 17592186425522 "answer-65f07f98-a8b9-5622-9b27-3d53b4b91fe2" 17592186425523 "answer-844474bb-952f-5653-9c05-58decf91ec4d" 17592186425524 "answer-aaaac3c2-cb51-55eb-b7b3-6b277435e640" 17592186425525 "answer-c93d79d2-a698-5d23-83bc-eaa0004f68c7" 17592186425526 "answer-d35be4b5-858a-50e5-916c-a8c257d81867" 17592186425527 "answer-d39bc26a-bf73-5514-8ace-4df9549e3b22" 17592186425528 "answer-dac293d3-2b8c-5f02-8569-0ff33e3f1998" 17592186425529 "answer-e263b34c-fdc3-56a1-821a-cd91cd1eecfa" 17592186425530 "answer-f232fefc-778d-57b7-9c36-9f38d8b9078a" 17592186425531 "answer-f23fa1b7-310e-5e39-a994-088b046f6326" 17592186425532 "answer-field-1bd2bd7d-81b6-570e-8fdd-b4fa401ea4d8" 17592186425533 "answer-field-5d59258b-b2f8-5954-823d-22bfd5f84b58" 17592186425534 "answer-field-a166156c-a351-5495-9912-8c241a9caedf" 17592186425535 "answer-field-dd714c02-0a09-5253-9229-c78cde01f445" 17592186425536 "answer-field-e53b86c5-f2cb-5dad-8677-36c6c80c81f6" 17592186425537 "answer-field-f5be0410-2431-593a-bcce-244299805303" 17592